v 3
d taxsim_py. Federal, state and payroll taxes with the same inputs and outputs as NBER's taxsim35
d
d Calculates US federal and state income taxes and payroll taxes for every observation
d in memory, reading the same input variables as NBER's taxsim35 and taxsimlocal35 and
d returning at least the same output variables. The calculation is done by the taxsim-py
d Python package (https://pypi.org/project/taxsim-py/), run in Stata's Python.
d
d Requires Stata 16 or newer, and Stata's Python able to import taxsim-py: add
d taxsim-py[readstat] to your Python environment, or create one with taxsim_py install
d (which needs uv, https://docs.astral.sh/uv/). See help taxsim_py.
d
d Author: Jon Rothbaum
d Support: https://github.com/jrothbaum/taxsim_py
d
d Distribution-Date: 20261010
